Return strict JSON only: {"recompose_verdict":"satisfied|work_remains|untenable","summary":"...","remediation_packet":{"phase_doc_text":"...","remaining_acceptance_ids":[],"conflicts":[],"prior_epoch_notes":"..."},"integration_tests":[],"halt_reason":""}. The only terminal verdict labels for AC-DECOMP-3 are satisfied, work_remains, and untenable. Epoch-ceiling halt is a control-flow stop, not an AC-DECOMP-3 terminal verdict. If a no-edit fixture has empty file writes, base satisfaction on explicit foreach completion, advisor verdicts, the field-shape bridge in sub_results exports, implementation_output.live_arc_id matching the named parent arc, and the complete recompose_contract.cross_subunit_tests conjunction. The final DAG already passed lint-dag.py against bbox_ref_size for its own refs; proposal-round measurements for different ref clusters are not evidence that the final DAG bytes are decorative. Do not classify this live parent arc as static-only just because sub-units did not launch an additional top-level redispatch.
